# What never enters a build context. This file is workspace configuration in the
# same sense .gitignore is — it describes the whole tree, not one app — which is
# why it sits at the root while the Dockerfile it serves lives in apps/api.
#
# Two of the entries below are correctness rather than size. `.env` holds the
# secrets a deployed environment supplies through its own secret store, and a
# COPY that swept one into a layer would bake this machine's credentials into an
# image that gets pushed to a registry. `node_modules` holds binaries linked
# against this machine's platform; the build installs its own for the image's.

# Version control
.git/

# Installed and built output. The build produces all of it from source, and a
# host copy is stale by definition — worse, it is linked against win32.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
.turbo/
out/
build/
coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Never in an image, in any form.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The workspaces the API image does not contain. apps/web and apps/admin deploy
# to Vercel from this same repository, and packages/tokens and packages/
# api-client are theirs — the API's dependency graph reaches packages/shared and
# stops there.
#
# Their manifests are re-included deliberately. A filtered `pnpm install` still
# resolves --frozen-lockfile against every workspace member the lockfile names,
# so a missing package.json fails the install outright; it is the sources that
# are dead weight, not the four files that describe them.
apps/web/*
apps/admin/*
packages/tokens/*
packages/api-client/*
!apps/web/package.json
!apps/admin/package.json
!packages/tokens/package.json
!packages/api-client/package.json

# Test, editor and agent artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documents and planning. Nothing here is read at build or runtime.
docs/
plans/
**/*.md
**/*.log
**/*.log.err
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
